"text": "This will explain to you how you can do the hard things and why do most people procrastinate. So imagine you want to improve any area of your life. For example, finances, and this will be your big pleasure. For example, tenants, your income. So here on this side is what you want to get. And here we have a pain. We have a price we need to pay, a resistance, a fear, a hard stuff, the boring stuff that we need to do. And here are we in the middle. And most people think that we go between pain and pleasure. Well, it's not really the case. Here on this side, we also have a pain. And this is the pain of everything staying as it is. And until the pain here is smaller than the pain of the resistance, we won't actually move it. No matter how big pleasure it is, we will still resist it. The moment this flips and the pain for everything staying as it is become bitter, then the moment you start to move instantly. We have to use both sides of this mechanism, both pain and pleasure, in order to get what we really want to be. So if you want to make a big change in your life, follow me and let's do this together.",
